{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"TelemetryEvent"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","title":"TelemetryEvent","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK14TelemetryEventO","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TelemetryEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"enum","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than a protocol hierarchy, which is what makes §19.2 rule 3’s “no event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"payload may carry a secret” checkable rather than aspirational: the case list is closed, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"case has a fixed associated-value list, and none of them is a dictionary. There is nowhere to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"put a token in a payload bound for a metrics backend — the type, not a review comment, is what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps them out."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hooks are invoked on the calling task, so a sink must not block: §19.2 rule 4 makes buffering"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the caller’s job so they can pick the policy. Every mature metrics library already buffers."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/TelemetryEvent","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8S